WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.370
On holiday, you pass a shop
with a sign in the window:

2
00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:04.930
Se habla español.

3
00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:09.590
Further along, an estate agent's
window says: Se venden casas.

4
00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.330
Neither sign names a single person.

5
00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:16.450
So what are these signs telling
you, when nobody is named?

6
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.030
In this mission, you'll
meet the passive,

7
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.400
where the thing comes first
and the action is done to it.

8
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:25.370
You'll see it built
from one verb, ser,

9
00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:28.050
plus a past participle that agrees.

10
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:31.730
The doer comes after
one small word: por.

11
00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:34.710
Then you'll meet the version
Spanish uses far more often,

12
00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:38.210
and decide which verb
form each sign needs.

13
00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:41.630
Your mission: read every
sign on the street.
